so  first up here what would you both say is  the biggest  difference between the way you  approached your work on the show  day one compared to this final season is  there any like  new tool in your tool kit so to speak  that you would credit to working on  sabrina  oh my goodness honestly it's so it's so  interesting because i feel like  when i started playing sabrina she was  she was young she was she was dainty she  was excited about  life and and in this one year she's  become  so so weathered she's weathered so  many storms it's like she she's an  entirely new person so just  getting to play that range of a  character uh has given me  just a lot um  a lot of valuable information  and i think just you know speaking to  how brilliant  everyone is from costumes to hair and  makeup you know  depending on whether i was wearing like  this fabulous ball gown or like a a fun  little blazer it felt like i would like  my mood was  always changing depending on what i was  doing  are you laughing at me gavin i don't  know  i just love you  anyway i just feel like she was just  really fun and i i really enjoyed  every iteration of sabrina i felt like  she she had so many different kind of  versions of herself and i'm happy i got  to play all those and experience that  and that gave me a lot to uh to work  with my own life  yeah i mean holy moly how do you even  sum up this kind of experience it taught  me so much  uh i approached the character with a  really  um uh rigorous sort of  discipline in the beginning because i  felt like i really needed to earn it  at some point in there i became a little  too relaxed in it all and and got a  little lazy because it's like you're  playing the same character and you think  you've got it  um and then there's moments where you  realize you don't because as an actor  playing a character  you never really do and you have to do  your homework so it taught me endurance  it taught me discipline it taught me um  how to slow down and enjoy 